TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan; Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan, Figure 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Information sources"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"The 60 km swath is inferred from 6,000 pixels at 10 m sampling, but no sensor focal-plane, field-of-view, altitude, or image-quality constraints justify that pixel count or swath."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"The 2,700 km ground-track spacing is an approximate equatorial same-day separation, not a complete revisit or weekly coverage analysis; orbit phasing, latitude, target geometry, daylight, clouds, and off-nadir imaging are not assessed."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The 10 m resolution and weekly cloud-free imaging requirements are stated as preliminary targets but are not yet supported by evidence that they suffice to detect bleaching using the cited method."}],"overall":"A strong preliminary report with a well-motivated Australian mission, a detailed and risk-aware project plan, and credible initial orbit work. The main next step is to validate sensor assumptions and quantify target revisit and coverage in STK.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":36.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The mission need, benefit to Australia, operator, user needs, goal and measurable preliminary requirements are clearly connected. Relevant references are provided. A minor weakness is that the 10 m resolution and weekly cloud-free coverage requirements are not yet validated against the imaging method or feasible orbit.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Give reef managers direct, repeatable observations of coral colour over the whole Great Barrier Reef"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Its customers are the Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Authority"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Deliver each image to an Australian ground station within 24 hours of capture."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":27.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"The Gantt chart is detailed and mission-sequenced, with completed/planned work, deadlines, float, explicit risks and contingencies, and relevant information sources. The plan connects orbit work to imaging and communications needs. Some task duration and milestone detail remains broad, but the project appears feasible.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Project work is divided into weeks in the Gantt chart in Figure 1"},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Week 10 is float as well as editing time: no new design work is planned in it."},{"where":"Information sources","quote":"Table 2 lists the sources I plan to use and what each is for."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"The submission includes useful orbital calculations, a preliminary coverage assessment, interpretation of the main feasibility trade, and evidence of an STK scenario. This is meaningful early design progress, though there are no simulation results or sensor/coverage validation yet.","evidence":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have also made first hand calculations for a candidate orbit, a circular sun-synchronous orbit at 600 km altitude"},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"A first STK scenario with this orbit has been set up, and its period agrees with the hand calculation."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":16.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report has a logical structure, clear headings, labelled figures and tables, and a mostly professional style with a reference list. The Gantt chart and tables are legible and useful. Some wording is informal or awkward, and several references are broad or incompletely specified, so presentation is not fully polished.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Project work is divided into weeks in the Gantt chart in Figure 1"},{"where":"Information sources","quote":"Table 2 lists the sources I plan to use and what each is for."}]}]}
